  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district (basis recorded as cash); governmental funds only. Statements from the Total Governmental Funds column (printed pp10-12 = trimmed pp4-6). Beginning/ending cash recorded as governmental fund balances rolled forward: 3,656,276 + 5,675,750 - 6,734,516 + 282,845 - 282,845 = 2,597,510. Receipts splits: 'Other local receipts' 6,164 = tuition 5,344 + local license fees 820 (General Fund budget schedule p8); 'Other' 17,285 = insurance adjustments 1,018 + non-revenue receipts 15,736 (General) + 461 (Nutrition) + sale of property 70 (Special Building). 'State receipts' 2,103,352 left as one state aid line (mostly property tax credit/homestead/state aid). 'Student support services' 581,542 split into General Fund 309,576 and Activities Fund 271,966 (student activities) per fund columns. Debt service is principal and interest combined (review). Transfers cross-check: General Fund transfers out 282,845 = Nutrition 141,045 + Activities 141,800. The General Fund budget schedule prints the transfer as '8000 Activities Fund support' 282,845 inside its disbursement total 5,504,043 (statement total 5,221,198), so it is recorded in detail as an other financing line (signed -282,845, printed_in expenditure) and the detail_totals entry includes other financing; Nutrition and Activities receipt totals likewise include their transfers in. General Fund combining schedule (p7, with Depreciation Fund and reclassifications) and budget schedule are the same fund; only the budget schedule (more detailed) is entered in detail. The Depreciation Fund (116,056 balance, no activity) is part of the General Fund; its schedule (p11) has no actual receipts or disbursements. State categorical (3500) and federal programs (6000) lines in the budget schedule are categorized as instruction, consistent with the statement's reclassification column (p7). No program-by-object exhibit is in the trimmed pages, so spending detail is 'not itemized'. Balance sheet is the cash-basis assets/net position on p3 (no liabilities). No business-type funds (Nutrition Fund treated as governmental as shown on the governmental statement). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
